+# slink-upr — SLink's fork of Universal Pokemon Randomizer ZX 4.6.1
+
+Base: `Ajarmar/universal-pokemon-randomizer-zx` tag v4.6.1 (`7f00eb866ed35c8fe3963f078b6a2e0979dc2b8c`).
+Purpose: randomize pureRGB (Red/Blue/Green, pinned build 7e7a4653) losslessly — load→save with every
+setting off is byte-identical, and every enabled category writes only its own species/level/item
+bytes (docs/purergb/PLAN.md §6 M5, §11.2 C1/D1). Vanilla entries are unchanged: for a fixed seed +
+settings the fork's output is sha1-identical to the 4.6.1 release jar.
+
+`Version.VERSION_STRING` is `4.6.1-slink1`; `Version.VERSION` stays 322 so `.rnqs` files interoperate.
+Build: `python tools/build_upr_fork.py` in the SLink checkout (javac --release 8 + jar; no build file
+upstream). Line numbers below are the ZX 4.6.1 file (`git diff -U0 7f00eb86 -- <file>`).
+
+Every new behaviour is keyed off the ROM entry (`LosslessMode=1` or a key that is absent on vanilla
+entries), so a vanilla `[Red (U)]`-style entry executes exactly the original code paths.
+
+## Patch 1 — lossless baseline (`Gen1RomHandler.java`)
+- `RomEntry.hasValue(key)` (after L131): presence test that does not plant `getValue`'s "or 0" default.
+- Handler state + helpers (after L332): `pristine` (ROM as loaded), `opaqueInternalIds`
+  (`NonDexSpecies[]`), `opaqueSentinel`, `evoSnapshot`; `lossless()`, `isOpaque()`, `pokeByInternal()`,
+  `fixedSpeciesByte()`, `bsEntrySize()`, `trainerClassCount()`, `snapshotEvolutions()`.
+- `loadedRom()` L357-365: build the opaque set + sentinel, snapshot the ROM (lossless only), snapshot the
+  evolution graph after load.
+- `savePokemonStats()` L745-767: names are never re-encoded on a lossless entry; the evos/movesets
+  repack (`writeEvosAndMovesLearnt(true, null)`) runs only when the evolution graph changed.
+- `randomizeIntroPokemon()` L2239: returns when the entry has no `IntroPokemonOffset` (D1 P0 defect:
+  the absent key resolved to 0 and wrote `rom[0]`).
+- `miscTweaksAvailable()` L2084: returns 0 on a lossless entry (every tweak is a code write, incl.
+  FASTEST_TEXT).
+- `setTrainers()` L1386-1399: the `ExtraTrainerMovesTableOffset` 0xFF wipe and the champion-rival NOPs
+  are skipped on a lossless entry.
+- `setTMMoves()` L1715: the gym-leader move write is skipped on a lossless entry.
+
+## Patch 2 — base-stat stride, opaque records, dex-0 sentinel
+- `BaseStatsEntrySize` replaces `Gen1Constants.baseStatsEntrySize` at L728, L759, L763, L1530 (the
+  literal `0x1C`), L1750, L1768, L2770 (falls back to the constant when absent; pureRGB = 35, Mew inline).
+- `populateEvolutions()` L1848 and `getMovesLearnt()` L1523 skip opaque internal ids (the 13
+  `NonDexSpecies[]` forms share a dex number with their base species and would otherwise pollute it).
+- `writeEvosAndMovesLearnt()` L2699-2713 + L2847: on a lossless entry every opaque id's record is copied
+  verbatim (ids that shared one record keep sharing it) instead of collapsing onto the null entry (D1 P0
+  defect 2). Note: pureRGB overlaps pre-evolution/evolution move lists, so a full repack needs 0xD4E
+  bytes in a 0x9F4 block; evolution/moveset randomization therefore fails with "out of space" on pure
+  entries instead of corrupting BaseStats (which follows the block; `PokemonMovesetsDataSize=0x9F4`).
+- Encounter/trainer/static readers use `pokeByInternal()` (L1018, L1048, L1069, L1084, L1099, L1124,
+  L1296, L1309, L1592): a dex-0 or non-dex id yields the sentinel, never a null `Pokemon`.
+- Writers skip a slot whose species byte held an opaque id when the ROM was loaded (`writeEncounter()`,
+  `setTrainers()` L1368-1382, `setStaticPokemon()` L1631): MISSINGNO in Sea Routes / the Rocket-house
+  static and the forms in trainer parties are fixed, never randomized.
+
+## Patch 3 — name tables as pointer tables
+- `readMoveNames()` L408-417 and `loadItemNames()` L2274-2303: with `NameTablesArePointerTables=1` each
+  name is dereferenced through its 2-byte pointer (`ItemNameCount` names for items).
+
+## Patch 4 — trainers (56 classes, $FE/$FD grammars)
+- `getTrainers()` L1269 / `setTrainers()` L1341 and the five name loops (L1927, L1950, L1966, L1995,
+  L2005) read the class count from `TrainerClassCount` (fallback 47).
+- `getTrainers()` L1293-1316: with `TrainerRecordGrammars=1`, `$FE` (level bit 7 = alt palette) and `$FD`
+  (custom-moveset id byte, then pairs) parse as special trainers; the tag, the moveset id and the palette
+  bits are carried on `Trainer.gen1RecordTag/gen1MovesetId` and `TrainerPokemon.gen1LevelFlags`
+  (`pokemon/Trainer.java` L37, `pokemon/TrainerPokemon.java` L7 + `copy()`), and `setTrainers()`
+  L1361-1382 writes them back verbatim.
+- `getTrainers()` L1320-1325: `TrainerTaggingDisabled=1` skips the vanilla class-number tag tables.
+
+## Patch 5 — statics
+- `setStaticPokemon()` L1628-1640: every `Level=[...]` offset of a record is written (was index 0 only),
+  so a double-encoded encounter (roof Zapdos: object row + inline immediates + floor object row) stays
+  consistent.
+
+## Patch 6 — fishing
+- `getEncounters()` L1065-1088 / `setEncounters()` L1174-1188: `OldRodOffsets[]` (several `lb bc`
+  sites), `GoodRodPairCount` (default 2), `GoodRodMonsOcean` (a second good-rod table, own EncounterSet).
+
+## Patch 7 — map names and hidden items
+- `loadMapNames()` L2469: internal-name row stride from `MapNameInternalRowSize` (default 4; pureRGB 5).
+- `getItemOffsets()` L2483-2514: membership in `HiddenItemRoutineEntries[]` (fallback: the single
+  `HiddenItemRoutine`).
+
+## Patch 8 — detection / entries
+- `config/gen1_offsets.ini`: `[PureRed (U)]`, `[PureBlue (U)]`, `[PureGreen (U)]` appended between
+  marker comments, generated by SLink's `tools/gen_upr_gen1_ini.py` (do not edit by hand). Header CRCs
+  0x929B / 0xCC68 / 0xC775 do not collide with any vanilla entry.
+
+## Patch 9 — verification (in the SLink checkout)
+- `tools/upr_lossless_check.py` — load→save byte-identical for the three pure ROMs via the CLI.
+- `tools/upr_write_domain_diff.py` — T6 audit: changed bytes ⊆ allowlist per enabled category.
+- `tools/upr_probe/SlinkProbe.java` — fixed-seed runs for the vanilla regression, `checkRomEntry` probe.
+
+## Known ceilings
+- Evolution/moveset randomization on pure entries fails ("out of space") rather than repacking.
+- Trainer tags are off for pure entries: gym/rival-aware options (rival keeps starter, type-themed
+  gyms) have no effect there.
+- Move/item names are read for display only; TM description text is not rewritten (no `TMText[]`).
+- Forms/MissingNo show as "MISSINGNO" in the log.
